            },
            {
              "text": "boolean",
              "kind": "keyword"
            }
          ],
          "params": [],
          "returnType": null,
          "description": "Whether light accumulates with headroom above 1.0, so that overlapping lights add up instead of saturating to white and a filter over the frame has something above the clipping point to work with. false under forward, which shades straight into the frame, and under lightmap on a WebGL2 context without EXT_color_buffer_float. The picture is still correct there - it clips earlier, and a bloom keyed on a threshold near 1.0 finds little to bloom."
        },
